# Tabs Setup

`chemicaljs/tabs` provides headless, composable Svelte 5 components for building a multi-tabbed browser UI with drag reordering, pinned tabs, horizontal and vertical layouts, autocomplete, and optional `localStorage` persistence.

## Components

All components are exported from `chemicaljs/tabs`:

* `Tabs` — root state provider and context.
* `TabBar` — tablist container supporting `horizontal` and `vertical` orientations.
* `Tab` — renders all tabs with drag reordering, animations, keyboard navigation, and middle-click close.
* `TabFavicon` — renders the tab's favicon with fallback content.
* `TabTitle` — renders the tab's title with edge fade overflow.
* `TabClose` — closes the tab (hidden automatically on pinned tabs).
* `NewTab` — button that opens a new tab and focuses `<AddressBar>`.
* `AddressBar` — URL and search input wired to the active tab and `<Autocomplete>`.
* `Autocomplete` — suggestion dropdown that automatically connects to `<AddressBar>`.
* `TabFrame` — renders isolated `<Frame>` panels for each tab and routes popups/`_blank` links into new tabs.

## Example

```svelte
<script>
  import Chemical from "chemicaljs/Chemical";
  import {
    AddressBar,
    Autocomplete,
    NewTab,
    Tab,
    TabBar,
    TabClose,
    TabFavicon,
    TabFrame,
    Tabs,
    TabTitle,
  } from "chemicaljs/tabs";

  let chemical = $state();
  let ready = $state(false);
  let tabs = $state();
</script>

<Chemical bind:ready bind:this={chemical}/>

<Tabs bind:this={tabs} persist {chemical} {ready}>
  <TabBar class="tab-bar">
    <Tab class="tab">
      <TabFavicon class="favicon">🌐</TabFavicon>
      <TabTitle class="title"/>
      <TabClose class="close">✕</TabClose>
    </Tab>
    <NewTab class="new-tab">+</NewTab>
  </TabBar>

  <div class="toolbar">
    <button onclick={() => tabs.back()} disabled={!tabs?.canBack()}>‹</button>
    <button onclick={() => tabs.forward()} disabled={!tabs?.canForward()}>
      ›
    </button>
    <button onclick={() => tabs.reload()}>↻</button>
    <AddressBar class="address" placeholder="Search or enter URL"/>
    <Autocomplete class="suggestions"/>
  </div>

  <TabFrame class="viewport"/>
</Tabs>
```
